# ADR 001 — Local-first architecture

## Decision

The application will use local storage as its primary source of truth.

Structured data will be stored in SQLite.

Files such as photographs, GPX tracks and FIT activities will be stored on the device filesystem.

External services will be optional integrations.

## Context

The application is intended for use during multi-day adventure trips where network connectivity may be unavailable or unreliable.

The application must therefore remain useful without an internet connection.

## Consequences

### Advantages

- Application remains usable offline.
- No dependency on a backend for core functionality.
- Fast access to local data.
- User data remains available during network outages.
- External integrations can be added independently.

### Disadvantages

- Synchronization becomes more complicated.
- Local storage must be managed carefully.
- Conflicts may need to be handled.
- Offline map storage can require significant device storage.